{{also|godspeed|God-speed|God speed}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|God-speed}}
* {{l|en|God speed}}
* {{l|en|godspeed}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|-}} phrase {{m|enm|God spede||may God cause you to succeed}}, from {{m|enm|God||God}} + {{m|enm|spede}}, singular [[subjunctive]] of {{m|enm|speden||to prosper}}, from {{inh|en|ang|spēdan}}, from {{m|ang|spēd||success}} (see {{cog|en|speed}}).

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|en|/ɡɒdˈspiːd/}}
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|en|/ɡɑdˈspid/}}

===Interjection===
{{en-interj}}

# {{non-gloss definition|The wish that the outcome of someone's actions is positive for them, typically someone about to start a journey or a daring endeavor.}}
#* '''1925-29''', {{w|Mahadev Desai}} (translator), {{w|Mahatma Gandhi|M.K. Gandhi}}, ''{{w|The Story of My Experiments with Truth}}'', Part I, chapter xi:
#*: I arrived at last, did obeisance to my uncle, and told him everything. He thought it over and said: '{{...}}At the threshold of death, how dare I give you permission to go to England, to cross the seas? But I will not stand in your way. It is your mother's permission which really matters. If she permit you, then '''godspeed'''! Tell her I will not interfere. You will go with my blessings.'
#* {{quote-book|en|passage='''Godspeed''', John Glenn.|author=Scott Carpenter|date=February 20, 1962}}
#* {{quote-journal|en|date=2007-05-12| author=Peter Steinfels| title=At Commencement, a Call for Religious Literacy| newspaper=New York Times| url=http://www.nytimes.com/2007/05/12/us/12beliefs.html| passage=And '''godspeed'''.}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[statement]] of [[wish|wishing]] someone a [[prosperous]] [[journey]], or [[success]].
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Evangelist, after he had kissed him, gave him one smile, and bid him '''God-speed'''.|author=John Bunyan|title=The Pilgrim's Progress|year=1678}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage="I'm wishing you '''God-speed''', Hattersley," cried Arthur, "and aiding you with my prayers."|author=Anne Brontë|title=The Tenant of Wildfell Hall|year=1848}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Rowland at the garden gate was giving his hostess '''Godspeed''' on her way to church.|author=Henry James|title=Roderick Hudson|year=1879}}
#* {{quote-journal
|en
|date=1884-11-02
|title=Thon
|journal=The Critic and Good Literature
|issue=44
|page=210
|url=http://books.google.com/books?id=9H_mAAAAMAAJ&pg=PA210
|passage=The new word has received a number of '''godspeeds''', some of which we quote.
}}
#* {{quote-book|en|passage=Eight years before he had seen his friend off at the North Wall and wished him '''God-speed'''.|author=James Joyce|title=Dubliners|year=1914}}

